{
  "dom_id": "step-q105973",
  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "If $Y={0,2,4,\u2026,140},$ which collection of subsets of $Y$ is a partition of $Y?$",
  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $Y$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $Y$ where every element of $Y$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{0,4,8,\u2026,140},{2,6,10,\u2026,138}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${{0,4,8,\u2026,140},{2,10,18,\u2026,138}}$  is not a partition because some elements of $Y$ (such as $6)$ do not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${{0,4,8,\u2026,140},{2,4,6,\u2026,138}}$ is not a partition because the elements $4,8,\u2026,140$ appear in both subsets.\n\n- ${{2,4,6,\u2026,140}}$ is not a partition because the element $0\\in Y$ does not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${\u2205,{0,2,4,\u2026,140}}$ is not a partition because the subset $\u2205$ is empty.",
